# CHAPTER THREE: THE RECEIVING ROOM
# 01:40 to 03:10. The frame and the figure. Hold. The archive. The room behind
# the deep end. Teodor in the office. Jad at the copy shop. Three o'clock.

=== ch3_start
@chapter 3 "The Receiving Room"
~ clk = 100
~ tick_n = 0
->> tick
@callable nell off "It's late. She's asleep, or trying."
@callable teodor off "Not answering just now."
@callable dima off "At work. Break at three."
@comp exchange
@set exchange
@cam inez_eye
@view inez
@acoustic tiles
@amb exchange_relays
@amb2 off
@xwin 1 view inez
@xwin 2 lamp off "HOLD"
@xwin 3 wave 200 "DOOR 200"
@xwin 4 text x "4B OUT"
@clear
It isn't one machine. It's a wall of them that have been talking to each other since before there were flats upstairs.
Racks of relays behind scratched perspex, rows and rows, like teeth. Circuit boards from four decades: green, blue, one a violent purple that somebody must have got cheap. Looms tied with waxed string and, further along, with bread-bag ties. Screws that don't match: brass, steel, one that is plainly a picture hook.
Cable tags cut from food packets. SEMI-SKIMMED. BEST BEFORE 14 OCT. SERVES 4. A pink ribbon knotted round one bundle. A tortoiseshell hair clip holding another.
One section, left of centre, is clean. Somebody dusts that bit.
And in a gap in the middle, where a board should be, a plaster Virgin about the length of a forearm. Her robe has gone the colour of old teeth. One hand is raised.
Inez takes off her head torch and hangs it on the raised hand. She takes a dry paintbrush out of her top pocket and goes over the statue's face, the folds of the veil, the fingers. Then she tilts the figure an inch, looks underneath at a grey ribbon cable pinned flat by its base, and sets it back exactly where it was.
~ saw_figure = true
@spot figure 0.40 0.20 0.20 0.60
@spot tags 0.02 0.30 0.30 0.40
@spot clean 0.68 0.20 0.28 0.50
-> ch3_frame

=== ch3_frame
* [ask][spot:figure] "Who is she?"
    INEZ: Celeste's.
    ARI: Who's Celeste?
    INEZ: My wife. Was. Is. In Lisbon, with her sister. We're very civil.
    ARI: She left her?
    INEZ: She said the Virgin didn't want to go to Lisbon. I think she didn't fit in the case.
    ~ k_celeste = true
    * "Do you pray to her?"
        INEZ: No. I tell her what I'm doing. You get into the habit, working alone. Somebody ought to hear it.
    * "Why dust her face?"
        INEZ: Dust gets in relays. She's the highest thing in the rack. Everything settles on her first.
        INEZ: And she was Celeste's. I'm not going to leave her dirty.
    * "What's under her?"
        INEZ: Ribbon cable. Two-twenty to two-thirty-nine. The clamp rusted through in the 2009 flood and she's exactly the right weight.
        INEZ: Take her out and the whole second floor goes quiet.
    -> ch3_frame
* [look][spot:tags] The labels on the cables.
    INEZ: People bring me things. I run out of tags, they bring me the tops off packets. The ribbon's Tobi's. She tied it on the line for 3B so she'd know which one was hers.
    INEZ: The clip's Bernadette's. She dropped it in the lift in 2015 and I never gave it back. Don't tell her.
    ~ k_tags = true
    -> ch3_frame
* [look][spot:clean] The clean section.
    INEZ: That's the part I rebuilt after the flood. Everything else is older than me. That bit's mine.
    -> ch3_frame
* "What am I sitting on, then?"
    -> ch3_hold

=== ch3_hold
@spots_clear
INEZ: You said you lose time.
ARI: When nobody's on the line.
INEZ: That's because nobody's holding you. A call on this frame is held two ways. Somebody's on the other end of it, or it's on hold.
INEZ: Hold's a circuit. It keeps a line alive with nobody on it. It needs something going through it, a signal, or it drops.
INEZ: When I started, the hold had a tape on it. The council's. Before my time they used it for more than calls.
* "For what?"
    INEZ: For people. The ones who came through here. They'd wait on hold for the room. Days, some of them.
    ~ k_hold_people = true
* "When did it stop working?"
    INEZ: Two thousand and nine. The flood. Nobody's waited for anything on it since.
INEZ: I'll put it back. Hang on.
She reaches into the rack. Her hand comes back with a strip of card torn off a packet label, SERVES 4, and she draws it through a pair of relay contacts, slowly, like flossing.
INEZ: Furred. Fourteen's always furred.
SOUND: A patch cord seated. A click. A hiss of old tape.
@xwin 2 lamp on "HOLD"
@music hold_tape
SOUND: A recorded voice: "Thank you for calling Ferrier Street Baths. Please hold. An attendant will be with you shortly." Then an organ, cheap and bright, four notes, and round again.
The same four notes as the ring, and one more. Then round again before it gets anywhere.
~ hold_fixed = true
~ k_hold = true
* "That's awful."
    INEZ: It is awful. It's the council's. Nineteen seventy-something. Everybody who's ever waited for anything in this city has heard that tune.
    INEZ: I can put something else through it. It only needs a signal. I've got a tape of rain on the skylight, from when I was testing the gutters. Or the pool lamps have a hum.
    -> ch3_hold_choose
* "I like it."
    INEZ: Nobody likes it.
    ARI: It's trying to get somewhere.
    INEZ: It never does, mind. They cut it for length.
    ~ pref_hold = "tape"
    -> ch3_casio
* "Can it be something else?"
    INEZ: It can be anything steady. A tape of rain on the skylight, from when I was testing the gutters. Or the pool lamps. They hum.
    -> ch3_hold_choose

