A long room lit by the strip over the counter and nothing else. Six copiers in a row with their lids up. The self-service computer glowing. A guillotine with a sign: ASK STAFF. DO NOT ASK TWICE.
On the counter, a stack of paper still warm from the printer. He fans it out for you.
Forms. The same form, nine times. Nearly the same. Different names in the top box, different handwriting, different signatures. In the box at the bottom, nine times, in the same neat capitals: ARI. And a telephone number that ends 247.
~ saw_stack_copies = true
JAD: Have you listened to the old messages yet?
if heard_inez_vm:
    ARI: Inez's.
    JAD: Right.
    ARI: How do you know there are old messages?
    JAD: ...Because I set up the voicemail. Inez did the line, I did the box.
    ~ k_jad_box = true
else:
    ARI: Some of them. Not yet.
    JAD: Right. Okay.
    ARI: How do you know there are old messages?
    JAD: Because I set up the voicemail. Inez did the line, I did the box.
    ~ k_jad_box = true
JAD: When you think of the coat. The coat from before. What colour is it?
* "Brown."
    JAD: Teodor's got you in brown.
* "Navy."
    JAD: Bernadette's got you in a navy mac. With a hood. Sensible.
* "I don't know."
    JAD: No. Nobody does. Everybody's got a different one.
~ k_jad_knows_msgs = true
JAD: It's been six weeks, near enough.
if k_six_weeks_form:
    ARI: Nell's form says the fourteenth of August.
    JAD: Yeah. It would.
else:
    * "How do you know it's six weeks?"
        JAD: It's on the forms. The dates.
        It's true. It's not how he knows.
        ~ k_six_weeks = true
    * "Six weeks since what?"
        JAD: Since the forms went in.
        ~ k_six_weeks = true
-> ch3_jad_format

=== ch3_jad_format
ARI: Sal sent me a picture. The same forms.
JAD: What's it look like? The top of it.
ARI: One page. The contact box is squashed at the bottom. Somebody's squeezed the signature line in under it.
JAD: That's the one-pager.
JAD: The council's one is two pages, and the second page is just the signature. So someone fixed it, so it'd go on one sheet.
* "Who?"
    JAD: Someone who fixes things.
    ~ k_jad_format = true
* "You."
    JAD: ...
    JAD: Yeah.
    ~ k_jad_format = true
    ~ ari_named_jad = true
* Say nothing.
    ~ k_jad_format = true
    The copier nearest him wakes up on its own, the way they do, and runs its lamp along the glass under the open lid, a line of light going left to right and back, over nothing.
-> ch3_jad_argue

=== ch3_jad_argue
ARI: I'm going to the lobby at half five.
JAD: Don't sign anything at half five in the morning in a lobby.
* "You don't want me there."
    JAD: I don't want you signing something you haven't read. Get Sal to read it to you. Every line. Get them to turn it over and read you the back.
    * "You're right."
        ~ jad_argue = "agreed"
        JAD: I'm right about that. I'm not right about much tonight.
    * "You've got another reason."
        ~ jad_argue = "suspicious"
        JAD: Yeah. I have.
        JAD: It's still right. Read the back.
    * "It's mine to sign."
        ~ jad_argue = "mine"
        JAD: It is. It's yours.
        JAD: I'm just... it's yours.
* "It's the only thing that says where I'm supposed to be."
    JAD: I know. I know it is. That's why I want you to read the back.
    * "You're right."
        ~ jad_argue = "agreed"
        JAD: I'm right about that. I'm not right about much tonight.
    * "You've got another reason."
        ~ jad_argue = "suspicious"
        JAD: Yeah. I have.
        JAD: It's still right. Read the back.
if p_kaye_thursday == "made":
    JAD: And don't promise Bernadette a Thursday you can't walk to.
    * "You don't like people relying on anyone."
        JAD: I don't like people relying on me. That's different.
        JAD: It's the same, isn't it.
        ~ jad_admits_contradiction = true
    * "I know."
        JAD: Okay.
    * "She asked."
        JAD: She always asks. That's what I'm saying. She asks and you say yes and then it's Thursday.
~ can_ask_made = k_fake_label or k_ask_jad or heard_inez_vm or ari_named_jad or k_jad_box
if can_ask_made:
    * [ask] "Did you make me up?"
        JAD: Can I tell you properly? Not in a copy shop at quarter to three. Give me half an hour. I'm coming back.
        * "Now."
            ~ jad_early = true
            A long breath out, through his nose, the kind you do before lifting something heavy.
            JAD: Yes. Sort of. I put your name on the forms. The name was on the council's sample. I didn't think anybody would...
            JAD: I'll tell you all of it. Properly. I'm coming back now.
        * "Half an hour."
            ~ jad_deferred = true
            JAD: Half an hour. Thank you.
    * Don't ask. Not yet.
        ~ didnt_ask_jad = true
JAD: I'm going to head back. It's a twenty-minute walk.
if not jad_wont_hangup:
    JAD: I'll ring you when I'm in.
    @hangup
else:
    JAD: I'm going to hang up, though. Sorry. I need both hands for the door. You've got the hold now, Inez said?
    @hangup
@avail jad off "Walking back from the shop."
~ gap_n = 4
->> call_gap
-> ch3_three

=== ch3_three
~ clk = 175
->> tick
It's five to three.
~ dima_due = (p_dima_call == "made" or p_dima_call == "maybe") and b_dima
~ teodor_due = p_teodor_three == "made" or p_teodor_three == "maybe"
if dima_due and teodor_due:
    THINK: You told Dima you'd ring at three. Teodor rings at three. There's one of you.
    -> ch3_three_both
elif dima_due:
    THINK: You said you'd ring Dima at three.
    -> ch3_three_dima
elif teodor_due:
    -> ch3_three_teodor
else:
    ->> ch3_three_quiet
    -> ch3_sal

=== ch3_three_quiet
@music hold_{pref_hold}
Three o'clock goes past on the hold. Somewhere upstairs, in 5A, somebody is lifting a receiver and putting it down again without dialling. You can feel the line go warm and cool.
@music off
~ tick_n = 6
->> tick
return

