=== ch3_dima_three
~ clk = 180
->> tick
@set bakery
@cam dima_eye
@acoustic bakery
@call dima
@view none
@amb bakery
~ p_dima_call = "kept"
SOUND: Two rings. Wind, a roller door, a radio playing somebody's idea of dance music.
DIMA: Three o'clock. You rang.
DIMA: I didn't think you would. Nobody does what they say at three.
* [look] "Can I see?"
    @view dima
    A loading bay, lit orange. Racks on wheels, tall as a person, every shelf full of trays. Dima's hand holding a roll that came out wrong, shaped like a slipper.
    DIMA: Seconds. We get the seconds. This one's a slipper. Look at it.
* "What are you doing?"
    DIMA: Eating a roll that came out the shape of a slipper. It's my break. The slipper's the best part of the job.
DIMA: So. What are you?
* "I don't know yet."
    DIMA: That's fine. I don't know what I am till about Thursday most weeks.
* "Something that came out of the phone."
    DIMA: Well. Everyone's got to come out of something.
* "I think someone made me up."
    DIMA: Everybody's made up a bit. My mum made me up and look how I turned out.
    DIMA: Sorry. That's not funny if it's true. Is it true?
    ARI: I don't know yet.
    DIMA: Then it's a bit funny.
~ told_dima_what = true
DIMA: I've got eleven minutes. Tell me something that isn't about you. What's the building doing?
* "Teodor walks lengths of the empty pool."
    DIMA: He does! Twenty. He told me once. He counts to a hundred on the chair after.
* "Inez turned the pool lights on for me."
    DIMA: She never does that for anyone. Well. She does it for the pool.
* "The lamp man got the lamp through."
    DIMA: Don't. I'll cry. I'm tired, I'll actually cry.
DIMA: Right. Break's over. The ovens don't care what you are either.
@hangup
~ gap_n = 3
->> call_gap
return

=== ch3_three_teodor
